  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Viasat obligated $322M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date across 123 awards, with an average award size of $2.6M. Obligations were up 17.7% year over year. The Department of Defense was the largest buyer, obligating $201M, followed by the General Services Administration with $119M. Other buying agencies include the Department of Homeland Security with $1.4M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $346K. Viasat's largest markets are Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $189M and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $75M, with smaller activity in Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $26.2M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $12.6M. Fiscal-year obligations show a multi-year pattern: FY21 $484M, FY22 $561M, FY23 $527M, FY24 $341M, FY25 $273M, and FY26 $322M. These figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Viasat's federal obligations trended over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "The FY21 to FY26 series shows variability with a peak in FY22 and lower totals in FY24 and FY25. FY21 obligations were $484M, FY22 obligations were $561M, FY23 obligations were $527M, FY24 obligations were $341M, FY25 obligations were $273M, and FY26 obligations were $322M. FY26 obligations are up 17.7% year over year. The current-year total is fiscal year to date and is a partial figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Viasat's top federal customers and what markets do they buy from?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $201M and the General Services Administration obligated $119M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $1.4M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $346K. Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing is Viasat's largest market at $189M, followed by Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $75M and Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $26.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
